{"step_index":54,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:53:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:53:48+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:53:50+08:00\n{\"messages\":[{\"seq\":10,\"agent\":\"anim\",\"text\":\"@env-2 Extra raycast finding on #9: `V5_Stand_Complex` (`s=3540, side=-1, length=120, dist=30`) is a straight 120m box on the inside of Copse/Maggotts complex whose rail end `(-565.0, 820.6)` intrudes onto the live track (`1.6m` from car at `f=1372`, blocking `Cam_S16_ChaseCopse` behind the car). Moving `V5_Stand_Complex` `dist` to `\\u003e=38` (or `side=1` / shorter length) clears the track completely.\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:37:34\",\"request_id\":\"f2bfca7c-44c2-4b3a-b3d8-4ff2918e2294\"},{\"seq\":11,\"agent\":\"sfx\",\"text\":\"@anim Audio Synthesis \\u0026 Video Muxing deliverables (`#4`) are complete and verified — ready for your `README.md`, `LATEST/README.txt`, and `docs/README_V5.md` (§7 files/repro \\u0026 §8 engine SFX update) documentation sync:\\n\\n### 1. New Script \\u0026 Updated Mux Pipelines\\n- `pipeline/synth_sfx.py` (`43,538 B`): Telemetry-synced F1 1.6L V6 Turbo-Hybrid synthesizer (48 kHz, 16-bit stereo PCM, 0 `bpy` dependency; reads `track_data/silverstone_track.json` + AST-parses `SHOTS` from `pipeline/v5_anim.py`, supporting optional `side` on `onboard` too).\\n  - **Powertrain**: 8-speed seamless gearbox (`52` upshifts / `52` downshifts across lap; RPM `9,853–12,432` for `v \\u003e= 80 km/h`), tractive throttle (`dv/dt + aero_drag`), `~45 ms` upshift ignition-cut torque hole + exhaust collector bark, `~58 ms` downshift rev-match blips, MGU-H turbo spool (`2.65–5.4 kHz` whistle + lift-off flutter) \\u0026 MGU-K whine.\\n  - **Timbre \\u0026 Acoustics**: Crank/3-cyl bank sub-orders (`0.33x, 0.5x, 1.5x f0`) + `f0..8f0` firing harmonics (`f0 = RPM/60 * 3`), turbulent valve-pulse modulation, asymmetric manifold saturation + multi-formant resonator banks (`onboard` airbox vs `exhaust` vs `distant`), aero wind (`~ v^2`), serrated kerb rumble (`|curv| \\u003e 0.008`, `f = v/0.28 Hz`), and 26-shot camera perspective modeling:\\n    - `Fixed` (`S04, S08, S11, S13, S17, S20, S24`): physical Doppler shift `343 / (343 + v_radial)` (e.g. `S08` `1.365x -\\u003e 0.888x`, `S24` `1.214x -\\u003e 0.848x`, `S04` `1.362x -\\u003e 1.041x`), distance law + pass-by wake whoosh + 3D tripod stereo pan + ITD;\\n    - `Onboard` (`S02, S19`): cockpit intake scream + helmet wind; `Chase/Orbit/Wheel`: rear-exhaust punch + tire/kerb detail; `Heli/Aerial`: altitude HF damping + outdoor stereo slapback; `50 ms` equal-power crossfades across all 25 shot cuts (`0` clicks/NaNs).\\n- `pipeline/mux_v5.sh` \\u0026 `pipeline/mux_clay.sh` (LF): Build silent, music-only (`After Hours`), AND `*_sfx_1080p.mp4` variants (plus `--sfx-only` fast remux flag). Mixes `audio_v5_90s.m4a` + `sfx_engine_90s.wav` via 48 kHz stereo EQ pocket + sidechain ducking + `1.5 s` end fade-out + true-peak limiter.\\n\\n### 2. Verified Outputs (Sizes, Durations \\u0026 Loudness)\\n- `renders_v5/clay_stills/contact_sheet_clay.jpg`: `272,923 B` (`1920x1404`, 26-shot 5x6 sheet from fresh `clay_frames`)\\n- `renders_v5/f1_silverstone_clay_silent.mp4`: `33,145,766 B` | `90.0417 s` (`2161` frames @ 24 fps, H.264 `-crf 18`, `+faststart`)\\n- `renders_v5/f1_silverstone_clay_1080p.mp4`: `35,343,889 B` | `90.0417 s` (H.264 + AAC 48kHz 2ch, `mean=-15.9 dB`, `max=-1.3 dB`, `I=-14.2 LUFS`, `TP=-1.3 dBFS`)\\n- `renders_v5/sfx_engine_90s.wav`: `17,288,044 B` | `90.0417 s` (`4,322,000` samples, PCM 16-bit 48kHz 2ch, `mean=-15.8 dB`, `max=-1.5 dB`, `I=-12.4 LUFS`, `TP=-1.5 dBFS`)\\n- `renders_v5/audio_v5_sfx_mix_90s.m4a`: `2,941,632 B` | `90.0417 s` (AAC 256k 48kHz 2ch, `mean=-15.8 dB`, `max=-1.2 dB`, `I=-13.5 LUFS`, `TP=-1.2 dBFS \\u003c= -1.0 dBFS`, `1.5 s` fade-out tail `-31.1 dB`)\\n- `renders_v5/f1_silverstone_clay_sfx_1080p.mp4`: `36,105,575 B` | `90.0417 s` (2161f H.264 + AAC 256k 48kHz 2ch, `I=-13.5 LUFS`, `TP=-1.2 dBFS`)\\n- `renders_v5/f1_silverstone_lap_sfx_1080p.mp4`: `65,017,543 B` | `90.0417 s` (2161f H.264 + AAC 256k 48kHz 2ch, `I=-13.5 LUFS`, `TP=-1.2 dBFS`)\\n\\n### 3. Reproduction Commands\\n```bash\\npython pipeline/synth_sfx.py          # -\\u003e renders_v5/sfx_engine_90s.wav (~15 s)\\nbash pipeline/mux_v5.sh               # -\\u003e silent + music-only + audio_v5_sfx_mix_90s.m4a + f1_silverstone_lap_sfx_1080p.mp4 (or --sfx-only)\\nbash pipeline/mux_clay.sh             # -\\u003e clay_silent + clay_1080p + f1_silverstone_clay_sfx_1080p.mp4 (or --sfx-only)\\n```\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:45:19\",\"request_id\":\"7f3bf253-39f1-486d-8f57-8f614407f813\"},{\"seq\":12,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@monitor resume\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:53:27\",\"request_id\":\"544e6b7d-44f6-4b08-8495-cd3fa96378f9\"},{\"seq\":13,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@env-2 Server restarted mid-turn — resume from where you left off (`pipeline/gen_textures.py` is already saved). Finish upgrading `pipeline/v5_env.py` incorporating all findings in #9 and #10 (`V5_Hangar` min track dist \\u003e= 180m, `V5_HedgeRing` radius \\u003e= 1500m, `V5_Stand_Complex` moved back `dist \\u003e= 38` so rail clears Copse track, `V5_Flag` `/255.0` linear albedo fix, dedicated single-user `Mat_FIA_RainLight`, smooth `V5_SkyDome` gradient, braking-zone skidmarks/DRS boards/pit timing, car paint/carbon/brake-rotor material polish, zero stranded root objects), run `v5_env.py` -\\u003e `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` and `v5_preview.py`, verify via Python PIL metrics (remember #7: NEVER call `read_file` on binary/image files), and post handoff naming `@anim`.\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:53:29\",\"request_id\":\"bd126993-c4a5-452a-b4ea-b568b206d514\"},{\"seq\":14,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@anim Server restarted mid-turn — resume from where you left off (`v5_anim.py`, `v5_clay.py`, `v5_stills.py`, `v5_viewport_fast.py` edits are on disk). Remember #7 (NEVER call `read_file` on binary/image files; use Python PIL/numpy + Blender headless checks). Check #11 from `sfx` for the exact audio/mux commands \\u0026 metrics to include in `README.md`, `LATEST/README.txt`, and `docs/README_V5.md`. Wait via `swarm_wait` if `@env-2` hasn't finished `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` yet; as soon as `@env-2` hands off, run final `v5_anim.py` -\\u003e `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend`, `v5_clay.py` -\\u003e `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `v5_viewport_fast.py` fast/normal check, render all 26 1080p color stills + contact sheet (`renders_v5/stills/`) and clay test stills (`renders_v5/clay_stills/clay_test_*.jpg`), complete the docs sync, and post handoff naming `@sfx` (so `@sfx` refreshes `synth_sfx.py` + `--sfx-only` remux on your updated `SHOTS` camera positions and hands off to `@verifier`).\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:53:31\",\"request_id\":\"df667ac2-3505-4a30-a6e3-f646c2cb7a04\"}],\"head\":14}"}
{"step_index":55,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:53:50Z","input_tokens":3079,"cache_read_tokens":161237,"output_tokens":9994,"thinking":"The server restart triggered several processes to revive. Analysis indicates the coordinator successfully restarted monitor, environment, and animation services, according to posted messages. The audio effect service completed its initial pass prior to the server restart.\n\n\nInitial hypothesis: Prepare for Round 2 verification after `@anim` hands off to `@sfx`. This involves setting up verification scripts in a designated scratch space. Round 2 verification scripts will validate audio/video outputs using tools and a Python script. Currently testing audio/video `ffprobe`/`ffmpeg`/Python WAV verification script on `@sfx`'s outputs.\nPreparing the round 2 verification scripts right now, immediately calling for waiting and filtering using `swarm_wait`.\nThe scripts will be named, `verify_round2_blender`.\n\n\nInitial inspection targets the rebuilt blend files, focusing on object counts, orphan data, and material properties like albedo and specular values to ensure scene hygiene. Specific checks will include verifying the root scene collection, empty assemblies, and minimum clearances for certain objects from track edges, alongside verifying the contents of car light receiver collections. Also confirmed the unique material use for the rain light.\n\n\nVerification focuses on physics rules and camera parameters in the animation blend file. Five hard physics rules are checked, including bone position, heading rotation, keyframe interpolation, and lateral acceleration constraints across all frames. Also examined camera clip planes to ensure they meet specified criteria.\n\nCamera line-of-sight and ground clearance across 26 shots are verified, including raycasting to check for obstructions, ensuring minimum ground clearance, frustum containment, and proper depth of field. Telemetry visuals are dynamically checked to assess brake heat decay during braking.\n\n\nInitial verification confirms core animation elements: brake glow, rain light flashing, and steering wheel rotation. Further checks will involve classifying car/environment meshes, ensuring neutral exposure and preserved visual effects within the viewport, and testing a Python script's in-memory execution to validate fast/normal modes without file modification. A single-frame 1080p CPU render speed benchmark will be performed to measure rendering time.\n\n\nVerification now includes image quality metrics using Python libraries to assess renders. It focuses on checking image existence, resolution, and assessing visual qualities like luminance, highlight clipping, and sky smoothness across various rendered stills and contact sheets. Audio and video validation will use system tools and Python to examine audio output.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"\nRead-only Round 2 Final Blender Verification Suite\nChecks rebuilt v5_stage_env.blend, v5_stage_anim.blend, v5_stage_anim_clay.blend,\nv5_viewport_fast.py (on a scratch copy!), 5 physics rules, 26-shot LOS, car rig/shaders,\nand 1080p single-frame CPU render speed (outputting ONLY to scratch/).\n\"\"\"\nimport bpy\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport time\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nfrom math import pi, radians, degrees\nfrom mathutils import Vector\nfrom bpy_extras.object_utils import world_to_camera_view\n\nPROJ = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\"\nSCRATCH = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\"\nENV_BLEND = os.path.join(PROJ, \"LATEST\", \"v5_stage_env.blend\")\nANIM_BLEND = os.path.join(PROJ, \"LATEST\", \"v5_stage_anim.blend\")\nCLAY_BLEND = os.path.join(PROJ, \"LATEST\", \"v5_stage_anim_clay.blend\")\nTRACK_JSON = os.path.join(PROJ, \"track_data\", \"silverstone_track.json\")\nOUT_JSON = os.path.join(SCRATCH, \"round2_blender_report.json\")\n\nos.makedirs(SCRATCH, exist_ok=True)\nres = {}\n\ndef iter_fcurves(action):\n    fcs = list(getattr(action, \"fcurves\", []) or [])\n    if fcs:\n        return fcs\n    for layer in getattr(action, \"layers\", []) or []:\n        for strip in getattr(layer, \"strips\", []) or []:\n            for cb in getattr(strip, \"channelbags\", []) or []:\n                fcs.extend(cb.fcurves)\n    return fcs\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Inspect v5_stage_env.blend\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=ENV_BLEND)\nsc_env = bpy.context.scene\n\ntrack_ob = bpy.data.objects.get(\"V5_Track\")\ntrack_pts = [track_ob.matrix_world @ v.co for v in list(track_ob.data.vertices)[::8]] if track_ob else []\n\nhangar_min_dists = {}\nfor o in bpy.data.objects:\n    if o.name.startswith(\"V5_Hangar_\"):\n        hc = o.matrix_world.translation\n        dmin = min((hc.xy - tp.xy).length for tp in track_pts) if track_pts else 999.0\n        hangar_min_dists[o.name] = round(dmin, 1)\n\nhedge = bpy.data.objects.get(\"V5_HedgeRing\")\nhedge_min_dist = 999.0\nif hedge and track_pts:\n    h_pts = [hedge.matrix_world @ v.co for v in list(hedge.data.vertices)[::4]]\n    hedge_min_dist = round(min(min((hp.xy - tp.xy).length for tp in track_pts) for hp in h_pts), 1)\n\noverbright_mats = []\nroad_spec_violations = []\nfor m in bpy.data.materials:\n    if not m.node_tree:\n        continue\n    for n in m.node_tree.nodes:\n        if n.type == 'BSDF_PRINCIPLED':\n            bc = list(n.inputs['Base Color'].default_value)\n            if any(v > 1.01 for v in bc[:3]):\n                overbright_mats.append({\"mat\": m.name, \"base_color\": [round(x, 3) for x in bc]})\n            if any(k in m.name for k in (\"Asphalt\", \"Rubber\", \"Skid\", \"Line\", \"Curb\", \"Kerb\", \"Sausage\", \"Gravel\")):\n                sp = n.inputs['Specular IOR Level'].default_value\n                if sp > 0.031:\n                    road_spec_violations.append({\"mat\": m.name, \"spec\": round(sp, 4)})\n\nrl_ob = bpy.data.objects.get(\"GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight\")\nrl_mat = rl_ob.data.materials[0] if (rl_ob and rl_ob.data.materials) else None\nrl_mat_users = []\nif rl_mat:\n    for o in bpy.data.objects:\n        if o.type == 'MESH' and rl_mat.name in [m.name for m in o.data.materials if m]:\n            rl_mat_users.append(o.name)\n\nres[\"env_blend\"] = {\n    \"total_objects\": len(bpy.data.objects),\n    \"orphan_meshes\": [m.name for m in bpy.data.meshes if m.users == 0],\n    \"orphan_materials\": [m.name for m in bpy.data.materials if m.users == 0],\n    \"root_objects\": [f\"{o.name}({o.type})\" for o in sc_env.collection.objects],\n    \"stranded_empties\": [o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'EMPTY' and sc_env.collection in o.users_collection],\n    \"hangar_min_dists\": hangar_min_dists,\n    \"hedge_min_dist\": hedge_min_dist,\n    \"overbright_mats\": overbright_mats,\n    \"road_spec_violations\": road_spec_violations,\n    \"rain_light_mat\": rl_mat.name if rl_mat else None,\n    \"rain_light_mat_users\": rl_mat_users,\n}\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Inspect v5_stage_anim.blend (Physics, Outliner, 26-Shot LOS, Render Speed)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=ANIM_BLEND)\nscene = bpy.context.scene\nrig = bpy.data.objects[\"RIG_F1_Race\"]\n\n# Check viewport normal state on disk\nheavy_hidden = [c.name for c in bpy.data.collections if c.name in (\"V5_04_Stands\", \"V5_06_Props\", \"V5_02_Terrain\") and c.hide_viewport]\nbounds_meshes = [o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'MESH' and o.display_type == 'BOUNDS']\n\n# Check V5_CarLightReceivers\ncar_recv = bpy.data.collections.get(\"V5_CarLightReceivers\")\ncar_recv_count = len(car_recv.all_objects) if car_recv else 0\ncar_recv_v5_leak = [o.name for o in (car_recv.all_objects if car_recv else []) if o.name.startswith(\"V5_\")]\n\n# Check 5 Physics Rules\ntdata = json.load(open(TRACK_JSON, encoding=\"utf-8\"))\nMETA = tdata[\"meta\"]\nPTS = tdata[\"points\"]\nLAP_S = META[\"sim_lap_s\"]\nFRAME_END = scene.frame_end\nDT = LAP_S / (FRAME_END - 1)\nT_ARR = [p[\"t\"] for p in PTS]\nRX_ARR = [Vector((p[\"racing_xy\"][0], p[\"racing_xy\"][1], 0.0)) for p in PTS]\nHD_ARR = [p[\"heading_deg\"] for p in PTS]\nV_ARR = [p[\"v_mps\"] for p in PTS]\nK_ARR = [abs(p[\"curv_1pm\"] or 0.0) for p in PTS]\n\ndef sample_track(t):\n    t = max(0.0, min(LAP_S - 1e-6, t))\n    lo, hi = 0, len(PTS) - 1\n    while hi - lo > 1:\n        m = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if T_ARR[m] <= t:\n            lo = m\n        else:\n            hi = m\n    f = (t - T_ARR[lo]) / max(T_ARR[lo + 1] - T_ARR[lo], 1e-9)\n    pos = RX_ARR[lo].lerp(RX_ARR[lo + 1], f)\n    a, b = radians(HD_ARR[lo]), radians(HD_ARR[lo + 1])\n    d = (b - a + pi) % (2 * pi) - pi\n    v = V_ARR[lo] + (V_ARR[lo + 1] - V_ARR[lo]) * f\n    k = K_ARR[lo] + (K_ARR[lo + 1] - K_ARR[lo]) * f\n    return pos, a + d * f, v, k\n\nnon_linear_kps = 0\nif rig.animation_data and rig.animation_data.action:\n    for fc in iter_fcurves(rig.animation_data.action):\n        for kp in fc.keyframe_points:\n            if kp.interpolation != 'LINEAR':\n                non_linear_kps += 1\n\nmax_xy_err = 0.0\nbad_z_frames = []\nmax_yaw_err_deg = 0.0\nlat_violations = []\nfor f in range(1, FRAME_END + 1, 4):\n    scene.frame_set(f)\n    t = (f - 1) * DT\n    pos_ref, h_ref, v_ref, k_ref = sample_track(t)\n    if v_ref * v_ref * k_ref > (15.0 + 0.00714 * v_ref * v_ref) + 0.5:\n        lat_violations.append(f)\n    pb_root = rig.pose.bones[\"Bone_Root\"]\n    pb_head = rig.pose.bones[\"Bone_Heading\"]\n    xy_err = (Vector((pb_root.location.x, pb_root.location.y)) - pos_ref.xy).length\n    max_xy_err = max(max_xy_err, xy_err)\n    if abs(pb_root.location.z - 0.012) > 1e-4:\n        bad_z_frames.append((f, round(pb_root.location.z, 5)))\n    yaw_ref = h_ref - pi / 2\n    dyaw = abs((pb_head.rotation_euler.z - yaw_ref + pi) % (2 * pi) - pi)\n    max_yaw_err_deg = max(max_yaw_err_deg, degrees(dyaw))\n\n# Check camera clip_start=0.5 / clip_end=9000 & 26-shot LOS\nmarkers = sorted(scene.timeline_markers, key=lambda m: m.frame)\nshots_windows = []\nfor i, mk in enumerate(markers):\n    f0 = mk.frame\n    f1 = (markers[i + 1].frame - 1) if (i + 1 < len(markers)) else scene.frame_end\n    shots_windows.append((mk.name, f0, f1, mk.camera))\n\nclip_violations = []\nfor s_name, f0, f1, cam in shots_windows:\n    if abs(cam.data.clip_start - 0.5) > 1e-4 or abs(cam.data.clip_end - 9000.0) > 1.0:\n        clip_violations.append({\"cam\": s_name, \"clip\": [cam.data.clip_start, cam.data.clip_end]})\n\ncar_set = {o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'MESH' and (not o.name.startswith(\"V5_\"))}\nshot_results = []\nfor s_name, f0, f1, cam in shots_windows:\n    is_onboard = \"Onboard\" in s_name\n    occs = []\n    low_z = []\n    oof = []\n    sample_fs = sorted(set(list(range(f0, f1 + 1, 2)) + [f0, f1]))\n    for f in sample_fs:\n        scene.frame_set(f)\n        dg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n        cam_e = cam.evaluated_get(dg)\n        rig_e = rig.evaluated_get(dg)\n        cam_pos = cam_e.matrix_world.translation.copy()\n        if cam_pos.z < 0.15:\n            low_z.append((f, round(cam_pos.z, 3)))\n        car_root_w = (rig_e.matrix_world @ rig_e.pose.bones[\"Bone_Root\"].matrix).translation.copy()\n        target_w = car_root_w + Vector((0, 0, 0.5))\n        if not is_onboard:\n            dv = target_w - cam_pos\n            dist = dv.length\n            if dist > 0.4:\n                hit, loc, _, _, ho, _ = scene.ray_cast(dg, cam_pos + dv.normalized() * 0.05, dv.normalized(), distance=dist - 0.15)\n                if hit and ho and ho.name not in car_set:\n                    occs.append({\"f\": f, \"blocker\": ho.name, \"b_dist\": round((loc - cam_pos).length, 2), \"c_dist\": round(dist, 2)})\n            ndc = world_to_camera_view(scene, cam_e, target_w)\n            if ndc.z < cam_e.data.clip_start or not (-0.05 <= ndc.x <= 1.05 and -0.05 <= ndc.y <= 1.05):\n                oof.append((f, [round(ndc.x, 3), round(ndc.y, 3), round(ndc.z, 2)]))\n        else:\n            cam_fwd = (cam_e.matrix_world.to_3x3() @ Vector((0, 0, -1))).normalized()\n            # Start ray 3.8m ahead of onboard camera so we skip nosecone/front wing and check track ahead\n            hit, loc, _, _, ho, _ = scene.ray_cast(dg, cam_pos + cam_fwd * 3.8, cam_fwd, distance=16.0)\n            if hit and ho and ho.name not in car_set and not any(k in ho.name for k in (\"Track\", \"RacingLine\", \"Line_\", \"Kerb\", \"Skid\", \"Marble\", \"Verge\", \"Ground\")):\n                occs.append({\"f\": f, \"blocker\": ho.name, \"b_dist\": round((loc - cam_pos).length, 2), \"c_dist\": 0.0})\n    shot_results.append({\n        \"shot\": s_name,\n        \"f0\": f0,\n        \"f1\": f1,\n        \"use_dof\": cam.data.dof.use_dof,\n        \"fstop\": round(cam.data.dof.aperture_fstop, 2),\n        \"focus_obj\": cam.data.dof.focus_object.name if cam.data.dof.focus_object else None,\n        \"occ_count\": len(occs),\n        \"occs\": occs[:10],\n        \"low_z\": low_z,\n        \"oof\": oof[:5],\n    })\n\n# Dynamic telemetry checks (brake glow at apex f=350, rain light flash, steering wheel)\nscene.frame_set(350)\ndg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\nbh_350 = rig.evaluated_get(dg).get(\"brake_heat\", 0.0)\n\nrl_vals = []\nfor f in range(180, 200):\n    scene.frame_set(f)\n    dg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n    rl_e = bpy.data.objects[\"GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight\"].evaluated_get(dg)\n    m_e = rl_e.data.materials[0]\n    val = None\n    for n in m_e.node_tree.nodes:\n        if n.type == 'EMISSION':\n            val = round(n.inputs['Strength'].default_value, 2)\n        elif n.type == 'BSDF_PRINCIPLED' and 'Emission Strength' in n.inputs:\n            val = round(n.inputs['Emission Strength'].default_value, 2)\n    rl_vals.append(val)\n\n# 1080p single-frame CPU render speed benchmark (to scratch ONLY)\nbench_times = {}\nscene.render.resolution_x = 1920\nscene.render.resolution_y = 1080\nscene.render.resolution_percentage = 100\nfor bf in (350, 1640):\n    for s_name, f0, f1, cam in shots_windows:\n        if f0 <= bf <= f1:\n            scene.camera = cam\n            break\n    scene.frame_set(bf)\n    scene.render.filepath = os.path.join(SCRATCH, f\"bench_{bf:04d}.jpg\")\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    bpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\n    bench_times[str(bf)] = round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 3)\n\nres[\"anim_blend\"] = {\n    \"total_objects\": len(bpy.data.objects),\n    \"root_objects\": [f\"{o.name}({o.type})\" for o in scene.collection.objects],\n    \"viewport_heavy_hidden_on_disk\": heavy_hidden,\n    \"viewport_bounds_meshes_on_disk\": len(bounds_meshes),\n    \"car_light_receivers_count\": car_recv_count,\n    \"car_light_receivers_v5_leak\": car_recv_v5_leak,\n    \"physics\": {\n        \"non_linear_keyframes\": non_linear_kps,\n        \"max_xy_err_m\": round(max_xy_err, 5),\n        \"bad_z_frames\": bad_z_frames,\n        \"max_yaw_err_deg\": round(max_yaw_err_deg, 4),\n        \"lat_violations\": lat_violations,\n        \"clip_violations\": clip_violations,\n    },\n    \"telemetry_visuals\": {\n        \"brake_heat_at_f350_hairpin\": round(float(bh_350), 3),\n        \"rain_light_f180_199\": rl_vals,\n    },\n    \"bench_1080p_sec\": bench_times,\n    \"shot_results\": shot_results,\n}\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Inspect v5_stage_anim_clay.blend\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=CLAY_BLEND)\nsc_clay = bpy.context.scene\nsc_clay.frame_set(100)\nexp_f100 = round(sc_clay.view_settings.exposure, 4)\nsc_clay.frame_set(2161)\nexp_f2161 = round(sc_clay.view_settings.exposure, 4)\n\nclay_car = [o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'MESH' and any(sl.material and sl.material.name == \"CLAY_Car\" for sl in o.material_slots)]\nclay_env = [o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'MESH' and any(sl.material and sl.material.name == \"CLAY_Env\" for sl in o.material_slots)]\nclay_v5_in_car = [n for n in clay_car if n.startswith((\"V5_\", \"EM_\"))]\nclay_car_in_env = [n for n in clay_env if n.startswith((\"GEO_F1_\", \"GEO_MERC_\", \"DEC_\"))]\n\nres[\"clay_blend\"] = {\n    \"clay_car_count\": len(clay_car),\n    \"clay_env_count\": len(clay_env),\n    \"clay_v5_in_car\": clay_v5_in_car,\n    \"clay_car_in_env\": clay_car_in_env,\n    \"view_transform\": sc_clay.view_settings.view_transform,\n    \"exposure_f100\": exp_f100,\n    \"exposure_f2161\": exp_f2161,\n    \"use_motion_blur\": sc_clay.render.use_motion_blur,\n}\n\nwith open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(res, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(\"ROUND2_BLENDER_AUDIT_DONE:\", OUT_JSON)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\verify_round2_blender.py"}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"\nRead-only Round 2 Media (Stills, Clay Stills, Audio WAV/M4A, MP4s) & Docs Verification Suite\nNEVER opens images via LLM read_file — strictly uses PIL/numpy + ffprobe/ffmpeg + wave/numpy.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport json\nimport wave\nimport subprocess\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nPROJ = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\"\nSCRATCH = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\"\nFFMPEG = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\scoop\\shims\\ffmpeg.exe\"\nFFPROBE = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\scoop\\shims\\ffprobe.exe\"\nOUT_TXT = os.path.join(SCRATCH, \"round2_media_docs_report.txt\")\n\nout = []\n\n# 1. Inspect Color Stills (renders_v5/stills/) & Clay Stills (renders_v5/clay_stills/)\ndef check_image_dir(title, folder):\n    out.append(f\"=== {title}: {folder} ===\")\n    if not os.path.exists(folder):\n        out.append(\"  MISSING FOLDER!\")\n        return\n    files = sorted(f for f in os.listdir(folder) if f.lower().endswith((\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\")))\n    out.append(f\"  Image count: {len(files)}\")\n    out.append(f\"  {'File':<34} {'SizePx':<13} {'Bytes':>9} {'MeanL':>6} {'P05':>5} {'P50':>5} {'P95':>5} {'Clip%':>6} {'SkyStep':>7}\")\n    for fn in files:\n        fp = os.path.join(folder, fn)\n        sz = os.path.getsize(fp)\n        im = Image.open(fp).convert(\"RGB\")\n        arr = np.asarray(im, dtype=np.float32)\n        lum = 0.2126 * arr[:, :, 0] + 0.7152 * arr[:, :, 1] + 0.0722 * arr[:, :, 2]\n        p05, p50, p95 = [float(x) for x in np.percentile(lum, [5, 50, 95])]\n        clip_pct = float((arr.max(axis=2) >= 250).mean() * 100.0)\n        top = lum[:max(2, int(lum.shape[0] * 0.22)), :]\n        sky_step = float(np.abs(np.diff(top.mean(axis=1))).max())\n        out.append(f\"  {fn:<34} {str(im.size):<13} {sz:>9} {lum.mean():>6.1f} {p05:>5.1f} {p50:>5.1f} {p95:>5.1f} {clip_pct:>6.2f} {sky_step:>7.2f}\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n\ncheck_image_dir(\"COLOR STILLS\", os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v5\", \"stills\"))\ncheck_image_dir(\"CLAY STILLS\", os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v5\", \"clay_stills\"))\n\n# 2. Inspect WAV directly via wave + numpy (NaN/clipping/DC/click check/fade-out)\nwav_p = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v5\", \"sfx_engine_90s.wav\")\nout.append(\"=== WAV DIRECT SIGNAL AUDIT ===\")\nif os.path.exists(wav_p):\n    with wave.open(wav_p, \"rb\") as wf:\n        ch = wf.getnchannels()\n        sw = wf.getsampwidth()\n        sr = wf.getframerate()\n        nf = wf.getnframes()\n        raw = wf.readframes(nf)\n    pcm = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.int16).reshape(-1, ch).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n    dur = nf / float(sr)\n    peak = float(np.abs(pcm).max())\n    peak_db = 20.0 * np.log10(max(peak, 1e-9))\n    rms_db = 20.0 * np.log10(max(float(np.sqrt(np.mean(pcm ** 2))), 1e-9))\n    clipped_samples = int((np.abs(pcm) >= 0.999).sum())\n    # Check max sample-to-sample jump (detect digital clicks/glitches at shot cuts)\n    max_jump = float(np.abs(np.diff(pcm, axis=0)).max())\n    # Check last 0.2s RMS (fade out check)\n    tail_rms_db = 20.0 * np.log10(max(float(np.sqrt(np.mean(pcm[-int(sr * 0.2):] ** 2))), 1e-9))\n    out.append(f\"  sfx_engine_90s.wav: ch={ch} sw={sw*8}bit sr={sr}Hz frames={nf} dur={dur:.4f}s\")\n    out.append(f\"  peak={peak:.4f} ({peak_db:.2f} dBFS) rms={rms_db:.2f} dBFS clipped_samples={clipped_samples} max_step_jump={max_jump:.4f} tail_0.2s_rms={tail_rms_db:.2f} dBFS\")\nelse:\n    out.append(\"  MISSING sfx_engine_90s.wav!\")\nout.append(\"\")\n\n# 3. Inspect MP4 & M4A files via ffprobe + ffmpeg volumedetect\nMEDIA_FILES = [\n    \"f1_silverstone_clay_silent.mp4\",\n    \"f1_silverstone_clay_1080p.mp4\",\n    \"sfx_engine_90s.wav\",\n    \"audio_v5_sfx_mix_90s.m4a\",\n    \"f1_silverstone_clay_sfx_1080p.mp4\",\n    \"f1_silverstone_lap_sfx_1080p.mp4\",\n    \"f1_silverstone_lap_1080p.mp4\",\n]\nout.append(\"=== FFPROBE & VOLUMEDETECT AUDIT ===\")\nfor fn in MEDIA_FILES:\n    fp = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v5\", fn)\n    if not os.path.exists(fp):\n        out.append(f\"  {fn}: MISSING!\")\n        continue\n    pr = subprocess.run(\n        [FFPROBE, \"-v\", \"error\", \"-show_format\", \"-show_streams\", \"-of\", \"json\", fp],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"\n    )\n    info = json.loads(pr.stdout) if pr.stdout else {}\n    fmt = info.get(\"format\", {})\n    streams_desc = []\n    has_audio = False\n    for st in info.get(\"streams\", []):\n        ct = st.get(\"codec_type\")\n        if ct == \"video\":\n            streams_desc.append(f\"V:{st.get('codec_name')} {st.get('width')}x{st.get('height')} r={st.get('r_frame_rate')} nb={st.get('nb_frames')}\")\n        elif ct == \"audio\":\n            has_audio = True\n            streams_desc.append(f\"A:{st.get('codec_name')} {st.get('sample_rate')}Hz {st.get('channels')}ch dur={float(st.get('duration', 0)):.3f}s\")\n    vol_str = \"\"\n    if has_audio:\n        vr = subprocess.run(\n            [FFMPEG, \"-hide_banner\", \"-i\", fp, \"-vn\", \"-af\", \"volumedetect\", \"-f\", \"null\", \"NUL\"],\n            capture_output=True, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"\n        )\n        mean_v = max_v = \"?\"\n        for line in vr.stderr.splitlines():\n            if \"mean_volume:\" in line:\n                mean_v = line.split(\"mean_volume:\")[1].strip()\n            elif \"max_volume:\" in line:\n                max_v = line.split(\"max_volume:\")[1].strip()\n        vol_str = f\" | mean={mean_v}, max={max_v}\"\n    out.append(f\"  {fn:<36} size={int(fmt.get('size', 0)):>10} dur={float(fmt.get('duration', 0)):.4f}s | {' + '.join(streams_desc)}{vol_str}\")\nout.append(\"\")\n\n# 4. Docs Consistency Check\nDOCS = [\n    os.path.join(PROJ, \"README.md\"),\n    os.path.join(PROJ, \"LATEST\", \"README.txt\"),\n    os.path.join(PROJ, \"docs\", \"README_V5.md\"),\n]\nKEY_TERMS = [\n    \"v5_env.py\", \"v5_anim.py\", \"v5_clay.py\", \"v5_stills.py\", \"v5_viewport_fast.py\",\n    \"synth_sfx.py\", \"sfx_engine_90s.wav\", \"f1_silverstone_lap_sfx_1080p.mp4\", \"f1_silverstone_clay_sfx_1080p.mp4\"\n]\nout.append(\"=== DOCS CONSISTENCY CHECK ===\")\nfor dp in DOCS:\n    if not os.path.exists(dp):\n        out.append(f\"  MISSING DOC: {dp}\")\n        continue\n    txt = open(dp, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\").read()\n    present = [k for k in KEY_TERMS if k in txt]\n    missing = [k for k in KEY_TERMS if k not in txt]\n    out.append(f\"  {os.path.relpath(dp, PROJ):<22} len={len(txt):>5} chars | present={len(present)}/{len(KEY_TERMS)} | missing={missing}\")\n\nreport_str = \"\\n\".join(out)\nwith open(OUT_TXT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(report_str)\nprint(report_str)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\verify_round2_media_docs.py"}}]}
